New version:
```ts
  const pos = vecAdd(s.pos, vecScale(vel, h));

  // Ground handling:
  // - 'atmosphere' / 'surface' are always clamped to the terrain (a landed
  //   ship sits on top of it. VTOL lift in the 'surface' regime lifts it
  //   back up).
  // - A 'space' ship collides only inside the surface disc of a landable,
  //   airless planet (TASK-87: that surface is solid — no tunneling through
  //   the planet body).
  // The sub-stepping above keeps the movement per step to 2 u or less, so
  // the clamp can't skip over the surface (no tunneling). On the ground,
  // a ship on an airless body (no atmosphere → no drag) is slowed by
  // SURFACE_FRICTION — that's what brings a high-speed airless approach to
  // rest, and where the regime machine resolves 'surface'.
  const inDisc =
    surfaceDisc !== undefined &&
    (pos.x - surfaceDisc.x) * (pos.x - surfaceDisc.x) +
      (pos.z - surfaceDisc.z) * (pos.z - surfaceDisc.z) <=
      surfaceDisc.radius * surfaceDisc.radius;
  const grounded = regime !== 'space' || inDisc;
  if (grounded) {
    const groundY = heightAt(pos.x, pos.z);
    if (pos.y <= groundY) {
      pos.y = groundY;
      if (vel.y < 0) vel.y = 0;
      if (planet === undefined) {
        const fr = Math.max(0, 1 - SURFACE_FRICTION * h);
        vel.x *= fr;
        vel.z *= fr;
      }
    }
  }

